    <item>
      <title>Message Queue using PAGI::FastAPI</title>
      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-queue/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-queue/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h4 id=&#34;disclaimer-image-is-generated-using-chatgpt&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DISCLAIMER:&lt;/strong&gt; Image is generated using &lt;code&gt;ChatGPT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Yesterday, I shared a post about &lt;a href=&#34;https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-apigateway&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API Gateway using PAGI::FastAPI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Today, in this post, I will talk about &lt;code&gt;Message Queue&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The latest release of &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/dist/PAGI-FastAPI&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAGI::FastAPI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is &lt;code&gt;v1.2.4&lt;/code&gt;. Having said, in the release &lt;code&gt;v1.1.0&lt;/code&gt;, we added the support for &lt;code&gt;Message Queue&lt;/code&gt; facade.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The distribution shipped with the simple memory-based message queue facade. There is even a handy demo app, i.e. &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/manwar/PAGI-FastAPI/blob/master/eg/memory_queue_demo.pl&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;eg/memory_queue_demo.pl&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s take you through the app source code:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>API Gateway using PAGI::FastAPI</title>
      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-apigateway/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-apigateway/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h4 id=&#34;disclaimer-image-is-generated-using-chatgpt&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DISCLAIMER:&lt;/strong&gt; Image is generated using &lt;code&gt;ChatGPT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Just released the &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/dist/PAGI-FastAPI&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAGI::FastAPI v1.2.0&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. This release brings it even more closer to &lt;code&gt;Python&#39;s FastAPI&lt;/code&gt; implementation. There are still pending things, which I have documented in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/manwar/PAGI-FastAPI/blob/master/TODO.md&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TODO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; document.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Right now, my brain is actively thinking about &lt;code&gt;PAGI::FastAPI&lt;/code&gt; all the time. I keep trying to explore what is possible to build useful utility with it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the &lt;a href=&#34;https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-websocket&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;previous post&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, I created websocket with it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this post, I will present a very simple &lt;code&gt;API Gateway&lt;/code&gt; demo. Actually this demo app is shipped with the release of &lt;code&gt;v1.2.0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
