      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;table-of-contents&#34;&gt;TABLE OF CONTENTS&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-headlines&#34;&gt;  1. &lt;a href=&#34;#HEADLINES&#34;&gt;HEADLINES&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;2-sponsor&#34;&gt;  2. &lt;a href=&#34;#SPONSOR&#34;&gt;SPONSOR&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;3-recap&#34;&gt;  3. &lt;a href=&#34;#RECAP&#34;&gt;RECAP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;4-perl-review&#34;&gt;  4. &lt;a href=&#34;#PERLREVIEW&#34;&gt;PERL REVIEW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;5-raku-review&#34;&gt;  5. &lt;a href=&#34;#RAKUREVIEW&#34;&gt;RAKU REVIEW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;6-chart&#34;&gt;  6. &lt;a href=&#34;#CHART&#34;&gt;CHART&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;7-new-members&#34;&gt;  7. &lt;a href=&#34;#NEWMEMBERS&#34;&gt;NEW MEMBERS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;8-guests&#34;&gt;  8. &lt;a href=&#34;#GUESTS&#34;&gt;GUESTS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;9-task-1-reverse-base&#34;&gt;  9. &lt;a href=&#34;#TASK1&#34;&gt;TASK #1: Reverse Base&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;10-task-2-rational-numbers&#34;&gt;10. &lt;a href=&#34;#TASK2&#34;&gt;TASK #2: Rational Numbers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;HEADLINES&#34;&gt;HEADLINES&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the &lt;code&gt;Week #386&lt;/code&gt; of &lt;code&gt;The Weekly Challenge&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am surprised by the dip in contributions in guest languages. Could it be the type of challenges we are working with reently? I can&amp;rsquo;t say for sure.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have group of regulars who consistently share the knowledge with us every week.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>PAGI::FastAPI &#43; WebSocket</title>
      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-websocket/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi-websocket/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h4 id=&#34;disclaimer-image-is-generated-using-chatgpt&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DISCLAIMER:&lt;/strong&gt; Image is generated using &lt;code&gt;ChatGPT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For last week or so, I have been playing with &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/dist/PAGI-FastAPI&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAGI::FastAPI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. This is my latest creation also my first attempt in creating async micro web framework.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have been, &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/pod/Dancer2&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dancer2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fan all my life. It has done all I wanted without any extra effort.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;While going through my old notes, I came across Python&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href=&#34;https://fastapi.tiangolo.com&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FastAPI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. I decided to port it to &lt;code&gt;Perl&lt;/code&gt;. Using &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/pod/PAGI&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAGI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, the job was half done already.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Access / Refresh Token</title>
      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/access-refresh-token/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/access-refresh-token/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h4 id=&#34;disclaimer-image-is-generated-using-chatgpt&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DISCLAIMER:&lt;/strong&gt; Image is generated using &lt;code&gt;ChatGPT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Couple of months ago, I shared my experience with &lt;code&gt;JSON Web Token (JWT)&lt;/code&gt; in the post titled: &lt;a href=&#34;https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/jwt-with-dancer2&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JWT with Dancer2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Having done that, I keep getting mixed up with &lt;code&gt;Access Token&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Refresh Token&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this post, I will try to get to the bottom of it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;access-token&#34;&gt;Access Token&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s like a wristband, short-lived, e.g. expires in &lt;code&gt;15 minutes&lt;/code&gt;. You present it at every gate, bar, or stage to get immediate entry. If someone steals it, the damage is temporary because it expires fast.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>PAGI::FastAPI &#43; DBIx::Class::Async</title>
      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/pagi-fastapi/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h4 id=&#34;disclaimer-image-is-generated-using-chatgpt&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DISCLAIMER:&lt;/strong&gt; Image is generated using &lt;code&gt;ChatGPT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Yesterday, I released &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/dist/PAGI-FastAPI&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAGI::FastAPI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;,&#xA;the first draft of new asynchronous, type-safe micro framework with dependency&#xA;injection and OpenAPI UI.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As soon as I released &lt;code&gt;v0.0.1&lt;/code&gt;, I noticed a bug in how routes are processed.&#xA;So I prepared a quick patch. While I was working on the bug fix, I thought of&#xA;adding an example that integrates with &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/dist/DBIx-Class-Async&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DBIx::Class::Async&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Just to give some context, &lt;code&gt;PAGI::FastAPI&lt;/code&gt; is inspired by Python&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;FastAPI&lt;/code&gt;.&#xA;I used &lt;a href=&#34;https://metacpan.org/pod/PAGI&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAGI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as the foundation of this implementation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
